   "text": {
    "L1": "Unknown substances should never be tasted or touched to test them.",
    "L2": "An indicator shows whether a solution is acidic, basic, or neutral by changing colour.",
    "L3": "Blue litmus turns red in an acid, while red litmus turns blue in a base.",
    "L4": "Turmeric turns red in a base and stays yellow in acidic and neutral solutions.",
    "L5": "Hibiscus extract turns dark pink in acids and green in bases.",
    "L6": "Pure water, sugar solution, and salt solution are neutral, so these indicators show no change.",
    "L7": "Washing soda turns turmeric red and hibiscus green, so both indicators show that it is basic.",
    "L8": "Now choose the classification that matches these indicator results."
   },
